<title>SPAIN: Spain has 121.9 bln peseta October c/a surplus.</title>
<headline>Spain has 121.9 bln peseta October c/a surplus.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1996-12-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of Spain gave the following figures (in billions of pesetas, surplus unless indicated by minus sign):</p>
<p> BALANCE OF PAYMENTS	    OCT 96	   SEPT 96 OCT  95</p>
<p>  C/A balance			121.9	     79.30    91.6</p>
<p>  Trade balance		    -94.1	   -236.40  -210.8</p>
<p>  Services			   230.8	    252.30   182.1</p>
<p>  Net tourism receipts	   272.4	    282.00   229.5</p>
<p>  Other services		   -41.6	    -29.70   -47.4</p>
<p>  Dividend income		  -39.6	    -66.60    -9.4</p>
<p>  Transfers			   24.9	    130.00   129.6</p>
<p>  CAPITAL ACCOUNT		   28.9	     33.30    86.9</p>
<p>  FINANCIAL ACCOUNT		  9.7	    -71.90   -21.9</p>
<p>  Spanish investment abroad    -60.0	     93.90    43.8</p>
<p>  Foreign investment in Spain  438.2	  1,234.30   171.2</p>
<p>  Spanish loans,deposits abr  -659.4	 -1,078.30  -434.8</p>
<p>  Foreign loans, deps in Spain 490.9	   -151.00   212.6</p>
<p>  Movement of reserves	  -200.2	   -170.70   -14.8</p>
<p>NOTE: The Bank of Spain said latest figures were provisional.</p>
<p>-- Madrid Newsroom, + 341 585 8340</p>
</text>
